The  driver provides support for a Network Virtual Service Client
(NetVSC), a virtual networking interface that relays  device  re‐
quests  to  the  Virtual Service Provider (VSP) in the management
operating system via the VMBus.  NetVSC  emulates  an  RNDIS  1.0
compliant  device  on top of a custom NVS protocol operating over
the VMBus channel ring.  Individual networking interfaces can  be
renamed by issuing a PowerShell command in the management domain.
In  order  to  enable sending and receiving of IEEE 802.1q (VLAN)
frames, the virtual port needs to be put into mode with the  com‐
mand.   The  driver  first appeared in and appeared in The driver
